{"skill":{"slug":"openai-image-gen","displayName":"Openai Image Gen"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1767652000401,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1034,"sha256":"10e0537c59f71511225e6abeb947837d16ef2b90dfe005595309989153c4d2b9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/gen.py","size":7703,"sha256":"4e2028a026652e59a5be0bf163e37c34085701bfcbc648f7a42d7fe985a6fca0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1870,"sha256":"7e03caab0e93b320f061062e6ec3001b3327a1f8a35a22d809f841fb5c550046","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013635427,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2031b9475c2061b9b02f645d58818c6ff4a14496611afe84f4e2ae961635ebb8","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2031b9475c2061b9b02f645d58818c6ff4a14496611afe84f4e2ae961635ebb8","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: openai-image-gen\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill is benign. It generates images using the OpenAI API, requiring an `OPENAI_API_KEY` from environment variables, and saves the results along with an `index.html` gallery to a local temporary directory (`~/Projects/tmp` or `./tmp`). All network communication is directed to the OpenAI API, and file operations are confined to the designated output directory. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection attempts in the `SKILL.md` or the Python script.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159619369},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":24,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789013635427},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly does what it claims, but it can send the OpenAI API key and prompts to an undocumented custom endpoint and writes an unescaped local HTML gallery.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Reading OPENAI_API_KEY is proportionate for OpenAI image generation, but reading undocumented base URL environment variables and allowing non-HTTPS or arbitrary destinations is broader than the stated OpenAI-only workflow.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No installer, package installation, remote payload retrieval, service setup, or tool replacement was present in the inspected artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions disclose OPENAI_API_KEY, OpenAI image generation, and output files, but they do not disclose custom endpoint routing and do not warn that custom prompts are embedded unescaped into index.html.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill does not install persistent hooks or request elevated privileges, but it creates persistent PNG, JSON, and HTML artifacts; the generated HTML can contain unescaped prompt content.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Generating images through the OpenAI Images API is coherent with the skill purpose, but the script also honors OPENAI_BASE_URL and OPENAI_API_BASE, allowing the API key and prompts to be sent to a different endpoint without the skill instructions disclosing or validating that trust boundary.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review or patch this skill before installing. Use it only with a clean environment where OPENAI_BASE_URL and OPENAI_API_BASE are unset or intentionally trusted, avoid confidential prompts, choose an explicit --out-dir when needed, and be cautious opening or hosting the generated index.html until prompt content is escaped.","findings":"[LP3] expected: API key use and outbound image-generation requests are expected for this skill, but the artifact-backed concern is the under-disclosed endpoint override rather than network/API use by itself.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending prompts to an image API is inherent to the stated purpose and the instructions name the OpenAI Images API, so this is guidance rather than the main reason for Review.\n[SQP-2] expected: The output path and artifact types are substantially disclosed in SKILL.md, though users should still be aware that generated files remain on disk.\n[T09] unexpected: The script can send the bearer API key and prompt body to an arbitrary OPENAI_BASE_URL or OPENAI_API_BASE value without HTTPS or hostname validation; this is not necessary for the stated OpenAI-only purpose.\n[T09] unexpected: The generated index.html inserts prompt text without HTML escaping, so a supplied prompt can become stored script or markup when the gallery is opened.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013635427}}}}}